() method is non‑destructive and the source indicator remains intact.'}]}, {'group': 'sma() - toString representation', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'barCount', 'value': 5}], 'expected': 'The toString() of the returned NumericIndicator contains the substring "SMAIndicator" and the period value (5), e.g., "NumericIndicator{delegate=SMAIndicator[5]}".', 'description': 'Checks that the wrapper’s string representation reflects the underlying SMAIndicator, aiding debugging.'}]}, {'group': 'sma() - nested SMA composition', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'barCount', 'value': 2}], 'expected': 'When a NumericIndicator first creates sma(3) and then on the resulting indicator calls sma(2), the final values correspond to a double‑smoothed series. For the base series [10, 20, 30, 40]: first SMA(3) yields [10, 15, 20, 30]; applying SMA(2) on that yields final values [10, 12.5, 17.5, 25].', 'description': 'Ensures that SMA wrappers can be chained and that each layer correctly uses the previous indicator as its source.'}]}]
